# Skeleton loaders — static text first, skeletons only for async

**Non-negotiable:** when a UI surface can load, the loading state must mirror the
final layout **and** render every fixed element immediately. A skeleton is only
allowed where the final value is unknown because it waits on a query, mutation,
permission check, media load, or route chunk.

Full checklist: **`skeleton-loaders`** skill
(`.agent/skills/skeleton-loaders/SKILL.md`). Architecture + route map:
**`docs/architecture/skeleton-loaders.md`**.

## Decision table

| Element                                                                        | Render now                                                                    | Skeleton   |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| Page title, subtitle, section heading, card title, tab label, column header    | ✅                                                                            | ❌         |
| Field label, helper copy, button label, legend label, empty-state copy         | ✅                                                                            | ❌         |
| Known icon / icon well (stat card, card header, nav item)                      | ✅                                                                            | ❌         |
| Known date, month label, day number, fixed count of static items               | ✅                                                                            | ❌         |
| Stat **value**, trend delta, async count, amount, name, email, status          | ❌                                                                            | ✅         |
| Async rows / cards / messages / table body / timeline clips                    | ❌                                                                            | ✅         |
| Chart plot, donut, mini calendar body, preview image/video, PDF page           | ❌                                                                            | ✅         |
| Action that only exists after data/permissions resolve (Edit, Publish, Invite) | ❌                                                                            | ✅ or hide |
| Description that concatenates a dynamic range (`Reminders · May 1–31`)         | ✅ static prefix + ✅ skeleton for the range only, or skeleton the whole line |

## Rules

1. **Static-first.** If the text exists in code, it is on screen during loading.
   Stat cards must pass `title` + `icon` to `StatCardSkeleton`; card headers use
   the real title/icon; tabs and table headers use the real labels.
2. **Skeleton the unknown.** Only values that come from data, async actions, or
   permissions are skeletonized.
3. **First load only.** Render the skeleton on `isLoading && !data`; cached data
   stays visible during refetch.
4. **Match the final shape at 375 / 768 / 1024+.** Same grid, padding, gaps,
   hidden/visible cards, and mobile/desktop variants. No generic spinner swaps
   inside a page body.
5. **State-aware.** Respect `?view=`, the selected tab, default section, empty vs
   data state, and permission-gated cards when choosing the skeleton variant.
6. **No extra cost.** Skeletons are static markup only: no timers, observers,
   fetches, or shared subscriptions.

## Do not ship without

- Route skeleton renders the same page chrome as the loaded page.
- Page-level loading keeps the header and swaps only the data region.
- Every stat card shows its fixed label + icon while the value loads.
- Card/section headings, tab labels and table column headers are real text.
- Known dates/months/day numbers are real text.
- The new/updated skeleton is listed in `docs/architecture/skeleton-loaders.md`
  and the route guide's Loading row when page behavior changed.

